1. VALIDATION ENGINE PURPOSE
The OneDraft Validation & Coordination Engine is the computational verification layer between the project model and the generated architectural documentation.
Its purpose is to determine whether a specific version of the OneDraft computational project model satisfies:
geometric constraints
project requirements
architectural coordination requirements
accessibility requirements
spatial requirements
building-code requirements
documentation requirements
interdisciplinary coordination requirements
and other rules registered against the project.
The engine does not modify the project model merely because a conflict is detected.
Instead:
MODEL
 ↓
VALIDATION
 ↓
FINDINGS
 ↓
ARIA ANALYSIS
 ↓
PROPOSED RESOLUTION
 ↓
COMMAND
 ↓
NEW REVISION
 ↓
REVALIDATION
Validation is therefore an independent computational function rather than an implicit side effect of drawing generation.

2. VALIDATION PRINCIPLE
Every validation result must identify the exact project state against which it was generated.
The minimum provenance chain is:
PROJECT_ID
 ↓
REVISION_ID
 ↓
MODEL_VERSION_ID
 ↓
CODE_MANIFEST_ID
 ↓
VALIDATION_RUN_ID
 ↓
VALIDATION_RESULT
A validation result without this provenance chain is not considered authoritative project state.

3. VALIDATION DOMAINS
The initial validation engine shall support:
CODE
GEOMETRY
SPATIAL
ACCESSIBILITY
LIFE_SAFETY
STRUCTURAL_COORDINATION
MECHANICAL_COORDINATION
ELECTRICAL_COORDINATION
PLUMBING_COORDINATION
SITE
DOCUMENT
DRAWING
REQUIREMENT
MODEL_INTEGRITY
Additional domains may be added without changing the fundamental validation architecture.

4. VALIDATION LEVELS
Validation operates at four levels.
Level 1 — Object
A single object is evaluated.
Example:
door.width >= required_width
Level 2 — Relationship
Two or more objects are evaluated together.
Example:
door
 ↔
wall
Level 3 — System
A group of coordinated objects is evaluated.
Example:
egress path
 ↓
corridor
 ↓
exit
 ↓
exterior discharge
Level 4 — Project
The complete project state is evaluated.
Example:
building area
occupancy
height
construction type
egress
fire protection
accessibility
site
documentation

5. VALIDATION RUN
A validation run represents one complete execution of one or more validation domains.
Conceptually:
VALIDATION_RUN
    ↓
RULE EXECUTION
    ↓
OBJECT EVALUATION
    ↓
FINDINGS
    ↓
SUMMARY
A validation run is immutable after completion.
If the model changes, a new validation run must be created.

