9. RULE IMPLEMENTATION BOUNDARY
Rules shall not be embedded directly into arbitrary API handlers.
The engine exposes a controlled interface:
Rule
 ↓
Applicability
 ↓
Input Resolver
 ↓
Evaluator
 ↓
Result Builder
Conceptually:
class ValidationRule:
    code: str

    def applies(context):
        ...

    def evaluate(context):
        ...
This permits the regulatory engine and validation engine to evolve independently.

10. RULE APPLICABILITY
Before execution, every rule is evaluated for applicability.
Example:
occupancy = ASSEMBLY
may activate assembly-specific rules.
A residential-only rule would therefore return:
NOT_APPLICABLE
rather than:
PASS
This distinction must be preserved.

11. RULE STATUS
Initial rule statuses:
DRAFT
ACTIVE
DEPRECATED
DISABLED
Only:
ACTIVE
rules participate in normal validation.

