63. ERROR ISOLATION
A failure in one rule must not corrupt the entire validation run.
Conceptually:
RULE A → PASS
RULE B → FAIL
RULE C → ERROR
RULE D → PASS
The run continues unless the error represents a systemic engine failure.

64. ENGINE FAILURE
A validation run becomes:
FAILED
when the engine cannot reliably establish the requested validation state.
Examples:
missing model version
corrupt geometry reference
unavailable code manifest
internal rule execution failure
database transaction failure
A failed run is never interpreted as:
PASS

65. VALIDATION CACHE
Future optimization may cache deterministic validation results.
Cache identity may use:
model_version_id
rule_id
rule_version
code_manifest_id
engine_version
Cached results must remain provenance-identical to directly computed results.

66. PARALLEL RULE EXECUTION
Independent rules may execute in parallel.
Example:
MODEL
 ├── GEOMETRY
 ├── ACCESSIBILITY
 ├── SPATIAL
 ├── CODE
 └── COORDINATION
The final aggregation waits for all required branches.

